# Deterministic line endings on every machine.
#
# The Expo runtime fingerprint hashes the RAW BYTES of eas.json and .gitignore.
# A CRLF checkout on one Windows box and an LF checkout elsewhere therefore
# produce two different runtime versions for identical code — and an over-the-
# air update only reaches builds whose runtime matches. That bit us for real:
# three hashes for the same tree in one afternoon. LF everywhere ends it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.p8 binary
*.p12 binary
*.mobileprovision binary

# Keys and certs are text, but must round-trip byte-exact.
*.pem text eol=lf
